oogle  we've been protecting our own systems  with two spectacular technologies over  the last decade  the first is recaptcha which defends  more than two million websites from  fraudulent bots  and the second one is a safe browsing  technology which defends over three  billion  devices from fishing in malware let's  take a look at these products in detail  some of the more common types of  fraudulent attacks we see  are account takeovers synthetic accounts  false  posts fraudulent transactions and money  laundering  recapture enterprise has built upon the  existing recapture platform that most of  us are familiar with  the goal of recapture enterprise is to  defend against these  various threats including but not  limited to scraping  fraud and account takeovers now we want  to make it very difficult for those  attackers to gain access  to your business to consumer services  and use them for malicious purposes  most importantly recapture enterprise  with recapture enterprise we can do this  while providing a frictionless  experience to your users and customers  the product acts as a barrier that is  placed for uh in front of your web  applications  where actions can be taken to stop bots  and fraudulent  activities from allah and and while  still allowing your users in  now let's take a look at the evolution  of google's recaptcha over the years  it got started with this quickly bit of  text that you're trying to read and  enter  and as god as bots got better um our  our defenses had to evolve and that's  why you see these click  boxes and crosswalks where the  challenges have become a little bit more  complex  and a lot of users actually have trouble  solving these and it's not the best user  experience either  um not only uh normally do we face  threats from ai but we also face threats  from farming  a large number of groups of people are  solving these challenges  for fraudsters um and now it comes down  to actually distinguishing the  transactions from fraudulent versus  non-problem transactions  and not just humans to bots the latest  version of free capture enterprise  is essentially a piece of javascript  that interacts with the user  um and gives you a risk score to  identify  whether the transaction or the user  interaction was alleged to make one or  not  so this means no text boxes and no  crosswalks  and just a snippet of javascript that  sits within your html pages  and there is no user interaction  required for the javascript to start  working  which means no friction from having to  actually solve the challenge  it's also based on the user's behavioral  analysis  on your website rather than relying on  just one form of challenge on your  webpage  so let's take a closer look at what's  included within recapture enterprise  now if you're familiar with recaptcha  weekly the enterprise version includes a  lot of  all of v3 and a lot more so it includes  an enhanced risk or  based mechanism which is based on  machine learning and is also  more specific to your website than just  generating bots  we also provide risk codes or reason  codes that allow you to better  understand  why we are detecting a certain behavior  as a as a bot or not now as a customer  you also have the ability to use the  annotation api to provide us feedback  whether or not a certain um as a certain  risk score that we provided was a false  positive versus a false negative  now remember that not all bots are good  or bad  it really comes down to understanding  your user behaviors and understanding  what your  business needs are now with recaptcha  enterprise we also have  mobile support with mobile sdks for  android and ios  we also have a new password leak  detection mechanism that's in early  access  we also have a two factor authentication  that can be implemented  for potential fraudsters um to further  assert their identity on your website  and finally since we are on the google  cloud platform  we provide sla and slo and also the  standard  gcp terms  now sensory camera enterprise actually  looks at the user behavior  and how they interact with the page and  synchronously in the background  the recaptcha servers formulate a risk  score based on the anomalies that we  have found on the website  now with the enterprise version we are  able to provide more granularity in  these risk scores that range between  zero to one  zero being a bad actor and one being a  good actor  now some bots actually have a bit of a  gray area that we need to provide  more details about and that's why the  enterprise  version actually provides your 10  pointer score where  which allows our customers to take more  precise decisions  on on their website and how they want to  apply  these protections on their website now  as an example you  almost always want to have a different  level of protection and security  around your high value pages like login  or check out  rather than a home page now let's take a  closer look at some of these  risk identifiers or reason codes we're  working on adding more and more of these  reason codes every day but here are a  few of them  now when a risk score is returned that  matches any behaviors  in the in this list and more we are  providing additional context  in the form of reason codes that can  assist you in tuning your responses to  your users and identifying  trends now let's do a high level  overview  of how all of these parts work together  um the page or the pages are actually  embedded with the recaptcha enterprise  now you can either have it on one single  page of your website or it could be  across all of your different pages on  the website the javascript will gather  the necessary data required to process  the risk score  and then that data is passed along as a  tokenized element  and encrypted um to the end user  now the predicted web application will  then receive that token when the user  actually interacts with the website  and then passes that token along over to  the recapture enterprise server  and then once the recapture enterprise  server is able to collect all of the  parameters and analyze it and provide a  risk score  it actually sends that risk or back to  your infrastructure  now based on the score you can actually  make a decision whether or not you want  to allow your user to continue  now the good news for current v3 users  is that the implementation is quite  similar  across recaptcha enterprise and  recaptcha v3 so if you're already a v3  user the transition is pretty much  just a line to point to a recapture  enterprise endpoint  so now that we have a risk or what kind  of action do we take  if a high risk score is returned it's  more likely that it's a real user  and there's you know you would want to  allow them to continue their journey on  your website  now if it's a low risk or depending on  the reason code you might want to take  either um a few types of actions you  might want to either reject that user  entirely and block them on your website  or you might want to provide a further  challenge like a two-factor  authentication to allow that user to  further assert their identity either way  you would want to  log all of these actions for further  analysis  now let's look at some success stories  around recapture enterprise  spotify was one of our earlier adopters  of recapture enterprise  we all know spotify and we love it they  were disruptors in the media industry  and transformed how we listen to music  some of the challenges that spotify was  facing included detection of bot traffic  and threats such as credentialed  stuffing  and abuse on spotify's website and apps  with recapture enterprise they were not  only able to effectively detect what  traffic but also protect and defend  against  threats coming from these bots another  one  another great example is empower  illinois empower  illinois is a statewide scholarship  granting organization that was created  in 2017 to serve children of illinois  through t