formation on  why a certain url was deemed malicious  based on some of the mentioned thread  types on the screen here  now this allows customers to take a more  educated decision  on whether or not to block these  malicious urls  now here's a remediation response for  example let's look at let's take a look  at the  sample workflow for weber's kpi once the  api returns the result if the url is not  a malicious one  our customers can choose to allow the  link to be then utilized on their  website  but if the url is malicious their  customer  then the customer can either decide to  block the  access to the website entirely by using  something like a web proxy  or flag the post as a malicious post or  even block the post entirely from being  submitted on the website  either way logging these activities is  always a good practice to allow scope  for future  analysis now that you've heard all the  awesomeness about recapture enterprise  and web risk api it's time to take  action  if you're facing any issues regarding  your fraudulent activities on the  website  we can help you with it please reach out  at  cloud.google.com recaptcha enterprise  and cloud.google.com  webrisk and get in touch with our sales  and technical teams  um to help protect your website  thank you for tuning in today

